               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="12XX">s. xiii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#g"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_4">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity or Christ Church.
                        </orgName><p>On flyleaf of MS 222: 'Liber Hugonis de Girunde de penitencia
                        magdal''. Hugh de Geround, monk of Christ Church, last appears in the record
                        on 4 January 1239, when he was accused of contumacy by the archbishop
                        following the forgery scandal (Greatrex, Register, 167--8); this book
                        suggests that perhaps penitence followed.</p><p>Identifiable in Christ
                        Church catalogue.</p><p> </p><p> </p><note
                        type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Cat. 1310</note></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Hugh de Gerounde (d. after 4 Jan. 1239), monk
                     of Christ Church, Canterbury.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Matthew Parker (1504--1575), archbishop of
                     Canterbury.</provenance>
